.TH INVF-PACK 8 "2026-09" "InvariantFS" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
invf-pack \- InvariantFS codecpack registry manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B invf-pack
.RB [ \-\-repo
.IR file://DIR | https://RAW_BASE ]
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-on\-volume
.IR MNT ]
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B invf-pack
installs, removes, updates and verifies InvariantFS codec packs from a pack
repository, and manages the per-family encoder alternatives. A pack is a
directory
.IR <name>/<version>/ "
holding a
.IR manifest ,
helper source and a
.I sha256
file; the repository also ships a machine
.I index.json
built by
.BR gen-index.py .
.PP
The repository source may be a local checkout
.RB ( file://DIR )
or a raw HTTP(S) base URL. Packs are installed into the host pack root
(default
.IR /.invariantfs/codecpacks ,
override with
.B \-\-root
or
.IR INVFS_PACK_ROOT ).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list [family]
List installed and available packs, optionally filtered by family.
.TP
.B search \fIterm\fR
Substring match over pack name, format id, provided family and description.
.TP
.B info \fIpack\fR
Print the manifest fields and, when installed, the install directory.
.TP
.B install \fIpack\fR
Install a pack and report missing external tools. The default conflict
policy is to
.B install but not touch an existing pack
that covers the same family; both remain and
.B alternatives
shows which is primary.
.TP
.B remove \fIpack\fR
Uninstall every installed version of the pack (and its legacy symlink).
.TP
.B update [\fIpack\fR]
Install newer versions for one pack or all installed packs.
.TP
.B verify [\fIpack\fR]
Recompute the sha256 of every installed pack file and compare it against the
pack's
.I sha256
manifest. A tampered pack fails. Signatures, when present, are recorded but
.B not
enforced.
.TP
.B alternatives \fIfamily\fR
List the packs that provide a family (installed and available), their
priority, and the current primary. The primary is the pack named by
.B use
if present, otherwise the highest-priority installed pack (then the
highest-priority available one).
.TP
.B use \fIfamily pack\fR
Set the primary pack for a family. This affects
.B future sweeps only
\- existing files are never re-encoded.
.TP
.B where
Print the resolved repository, install root and the pack search order.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-repo " spec"
Repository location:
.I file:///path
or
.IR https://host/raw\-base .
Defaults to
.IR INVFS_PACK_REPO ,
then the upstream GitHub raw URL.
.TP
.BI \-\-root " dir"
Install root (host). Default
.IR /.invariantfs/codecpacks .
.TP
.BI \-\-on\-volume " mnt"
Install under
.IR <mnt>/.invariantfs/codecpacks
for self-hosting / root-mode boots. The argument must be a mounted directory;
mount the volume image first.
.TP
.B \-\-version " v"
Select an exact pack version at install time.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /.invariantfs/codecpacks
Host pack root (trusted, admin-provided). Each pack lands at
.IR <root>/<name>/<version>/ ;
a legacy
.I <root>/<name>.codecpack
symlink is created for the v1 engine probe.
.TP
.I /.invariantfs/codecpacks/alternatives.conf
Per-family primary selection written by
.BR use .
.TP
.I $INVFS_CODECPACKS
Colon-separated additional pack search directories (engine side).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B INVFS_PACK_REPO
Default repository when
.B \-\-repo
is omitted.
.TP
.B INVFS_PACK_ROOT
Default install root when
.B \-\-root
and
.B \-\-on\-volume
are omitted.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; non-zero when a pack is not found, a sha256 check fails, an
external dependency check refuses, or an I/O error occurs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR invf-sweep (8),
.BR invf-fuse (8),
.BR invarifs (7)
